What does this log?

```js
const { a = 1, b = 2 } = { a: null };
console.log(a, b);
```

What does this log?

```js
const m = new Map();
m.set(1, 'num').set('1', 'str');
const o = {};
o[1] = 'num';
o['1'] = 'str';
console.log(m.size, Object.keys(o).length);
```

What does this log?

```js
const arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
arr.length = 2;
arr[4] = 9;
console.log(arr.length, arr[3]);
```

Which statements about `rest` are true after this code runs? (Choose two.)

```js
const base = { a: 1, b: 2 };
const obj = Object.create(base);
obj.c = 3;
Object.defineProperty(obj, 'd', { value: 4, enumerable: false });
const { c, ...rest } = obj;
```

What does this log?

```js
const arr = [1, 2, 3];
const b = arr.with(-1, 9);
console.log(arr.at(-1), b.at(-1), arr === b);
```

What is `doubled` after this runs?

```js
const prices = { apple: 2, pear: 3 };
const doubled = Object.fromEntries(
  Object.entries(prices).map(([k, v]) => [k, v * 2])
);
```

What does this log?

```js
const a = [1, , 3];
const doubled = a.map(x => x * 2);
console.log(doubled.length, Object.keys(doubled));
```

What does this log?

```js
const g = Object.groupBy([1, 2, 3, 4], n => (n % 2 ? 'odd' : 'even'));
console.log(Object.keys(g), typeof g.hasOwnProperty);
```

Put the keys in the order `Object.keys(o)` returns them.

```js
const o = { b: 1, 2: 'x', a: 2, 1: 'y' };
o.c = 3;
```

In a current browser or Node 22+, what does this log?

```js
const a = new Set([1, 2]);
const b = new Set([2, 3]);
const u = a.union(b);
console.log([...u], a.size);
```

What happens when this runs?

```js
const arrayLike = { length: 2, 0: 'a', 1: 'b' };
const x = Array.from(arrayLike);
const y = [...arrayLike];
```

What does this log?

```js
const state = { user: { name: 'Ada' }, tags: ['x'] };
const next = { ...state, tags: [...state.tags, 'y'] };
next.user.name = 'Grace';
console.log(state.user.name, state.tags.length);
```

This code is in an ES module. What happens?

```js
const counts = ['a', 'b', 'a'].reduce(
  (acc, k) => (acc[k] = (acc[k] || 0) + 1),
  {}
);
```

What does this log?

```js
const a = [];
a[2 ** 32 - 1] = 'x';
console.log(a.length, Object.keys(a));
```

What does this log?

```js
const a = [3, undefined, , 1];
a.sort();
console.log(a.length, 2 in a, 3 in a);
```

What does this log?

```js
const buf = new ArrayBuffer(4);
const u8 = new Uint8Array(buf);
const u32 = new Uint32Array(buf);
u32[0] = 1;
console.log(u8[0], u8[3]);
```

Put the values in the order this loop logs them.

```js
const s = new Set(['a', 'b', 'c']);
for (const x of s) {
  console.log(x);
  if (x === 'a') {
    s.delete('b');
    s.add('b');
  }
}
```
